# Keep rules for the shipped APK. AGP 9 supplies the platform rules and every library brings its
# own, so this file exists for the one thing neither can know about: a class this app reaches by
# name rather than by symbol.
#
# Glance identifies a widget by its GlanceAppWidget subclass's *canonical name*. `updateAll` asks
# GlanceAppWidgetManager for the widget ids belonging to `javaClass`, and that manager keeps a
# DataStore mapping each manifest receiver to the name of the widget class it hosts — written when
# a receiver's onUpdate runs, read on every refresh, and persisted across app updates.
#
# These three classes are otherwise identical in shape: same supertype, same `sizeMode`, same
# two-line `provideGlance` differing only in which composable it names. R8 duly merged all three
# into one class, so all three receivers recorded the same provider name, every `updateAll`
# resolved to all three widget ids, and each of the three widgets on a home screen drew whichever
# one had been refreshed last. Nothing crashed and no test could see it: unit tests run on the JVM
# against unshrunk classes, and a merged class is still perfectly functional — it just answers to
# one name where the app needs three.
#
# Keeping the original names rather than merely distinct ones is deliberate, for the same reason
# HeartbeatWorker keeps its: the mapping outlives the install that wrote it, so a name that moves
# between versions leaves the stored one pointing at nothing, and `getGlanceIds` then returns an
# empty list and quietly stops updating that widget.
#
# .github/scripts/r8-keep-check.py asserts all three survive under these names on every push.
-keep class it.eldavo.ylih.widget.LifetimeWidget
-keep class it.eldavo.ylih.widget.ActivityWidget
-keep class it.eldavo.ylih.widget.ChartWidget
